# Transient agent worktrees (created by the build orchestrator)
.claude/worktrees/

# Live coordination state for parallel sessions (the groepschat: chat log, claims, session
# files, BOARD.md). See .claude/skills/groepschat/SKILL.md, which IS tracked — the protocol is
# project convention, the state is not. Deliberately ignored for two reasons: a chat log
# committed across 8 concurrent branches would conflict on every append, and the durable record
# already has homes (backlog/, backlog/worklogs/<story>/, docs/adr/). Always reach it by the
# absolute path C:\source\Jaarplanner\.claude\coordination — worktrees sit below it, so a
# relative path would give each worktree a private copy and coordinate nothing.
.claude/coordination/

# Local data of the AI eval runner (TB-004): real evalsets hold a school's own subthema's and gold links, and the
# reports quote them. This repository is public, so none of it may be committed. Only the fictional
# backend/tools/Jaarplanner.Eval/voorbeeld-evalset.json is tracked.
/eval-data/

# Local secrets / environment — never commit real credentials (Art. VI.4)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Playwright MCP session artifacts (console logs, page snapshots) — written next to
# the repo root when a wireframe is reviewed in a browser; regenerated on demand.
.playwright-mcp/

# TEMPORARY, remove together with the folder. Debris from moving the repo root up out
# of C:\source\Jaarplanner\Jaarplanner (b2257f7); a root-level directory named
# "Jaarplanner" inside this repo is never legitimate. It is now empty of files — only
# an undeletable `docs/ux` directory chain remains, still held by an editor process —
# so this pattern is prophylactic, not describing an active leak. It earned its place:
# regenerated obj/ artifacts under it were swept into a commit by `git add -A` (96aa434,
# undone in 2081055). Delete the folder and this block once the handle is released.
/Jaarplanner/

# Screenshot of the approved E3-10 kalender wireframe, captured to the working dir by a
# browser session. Untracked deliberately (it was committed by accident in 96aa434 and
# removed in 369fee5), and ignored so the next `git add -A` cannot re-stage it. If it is
# worth keeping as approval evidence it belongs under docs/ux/wireframes/ with a
# reference from e3-10-kalender.md — not loose at the repo root.
/wireframe-desktop.png

# Build output of infra/deploy-app.ps1: the published API with the frontend bundle, and the zip it deploys (ADR-0034).
/artifacts/

# A dotnet workload log, written into a directory named after whatever argument the CLI took for a path. On
# 2026-09-15 that argument was a connection string, so the directory name carried a local database password and a
# `git add` staged it (FB-001; caught and amended before any push). Ignored so the next mishap stays out of the index.
**/Microsoft.NET.Workload_*.log

# Test run artifacts (trx logs, coverage) — generated by `dotnet test --logger trx`.
TestResults/
*.trx
